Self assesment measurements have been generated by the ngcc_bench program with the aid of a custom shell script.
run-bench.sh compiles all the implementations as .so libraries, then invokes ngcc_bench to test and measure the implementation.

Testing an implementation generates JSON reports in english and chinese for 128, 256 and 512 bit levels.

NOTE that seeds in Facto-DSA .so libraries are dynamically generated by OS entropy manager.

But before setting dynamic seed in the code, we used this one to generate the test results:

seedseedseedseedseedseedseedseedseedseedseedseedseedseedseedseed (IN ASCII)

You can hardcode it in the implementation code, as it now uses dynamic seeding, not fixed one.
